[Applause]  [Music]  video games have been a great way to  stay busy these last few months and that  won't be changing in July the coming  month has a bunch of hot new games from  big-name developers that I know I can't  wait to play and I bet you'll find  something to get hyped for too so let's  break down some of the biggest games of  July flying out of the gate first is  Marvel's Ironman VR if you've ever  wanted to suit up like Tony the of the  comic book one not me now's your chance  the game actually has a new suit called  the impulse armor but you'll still be  able to see Friday in your HUD as you  zoom through the sky and fire your  repulsor beams at enemies there might  not be many new superhero movies out  right now but you can still play as one  on psvr on Friday July 3rd speaking of  firing off weapons in the sky let's talk  about rocket arena as the name might  imply this 3v3 team shooter arms you  with nothing but rocket launchers each  character has their own special kind of  rocket though you can level them up to  get new stat boosts and effects - and of  course you'll also have to dodge all the  rockets headed your way  they'll be crashing on the ps4 Xbox one  and PC on Tuesday the 14th and now we'll  move from ranged weapons to the up close  and personal stuff with ghosts of  Tsushima this ps4 exclusive sees the  samurai jinn defending his Island for  Mongol invaders using a combination of  in-your-face katana combat and stealth  the Mongol soldiers are pretty fast with  their own blades so you'll have to  master different stances and counters to  deal with them  sucker punches next adventure is  launching on Friday the 17th and I dunno  what crossover I'd love to see down the  road  mario has to deal with invaders of his  own in paper mario the origami king the  latest entry in the series sees the  Mushroom Kingdom under siege once again  this time by the titular origami king  Ollie the origami style comes into play  as you explore the world bending and  folding things to solve puzzles and  collect coins there's also a new ring  based combat system that challenges you  to line up enemies or make your way to a  bosses weak point you can see it in  action on intend o switch on the 17th  and lastly you can play as the invader  yourself and destroy all humans this  remake puts you in the space boots of  Krypto who sent to a town in the  Midwestern United States to terrorize  the people and harvest their DNA using  all sorts of alien weapons and gadgets  it looks better than the old game of  course but it also includes cut content  from the original you can see the new  stuff on ps4 Xbox one and PC on Tuesday  the 28th and those are some of the  hottest games launching all month long  as always remember that release dates  are based on retailer listings and are  subject to change thanks for watching  everyone and I'll be back with a closer  look at more July games next Sunday  [Music]

